{
  "description": "T1 - Beech - To crown reduce mature Beech tree located along the right-hand boundary by approximately 2.5m in height and 2.0m in lateral spread, leaving a residual height of approximately 16m.\rThe tree has a significant Ganoderma fungal bracket present at a major union, which may indicate internal decay and potential structural weakness. The proposed reduction is intended to reduce the overall sail area and wind loading on the tree, thereby helping to mitigate the risk of structural failure.\r(TPO 05, 2017)",
